9452	{"artifactId":"LLD-c00559b7e38bb6ce-s1","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-c00559b7e38bb6ce-s1-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-11T13:08:02.139Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"pass","summary":"review: pass","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"pass","findings":[{"claimId":"fix-targets-defect.1","ref":"fix-targets-defect","item":"fix-targets-defect","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The root cause is that both work-item head readers (resolve.ts listEpicHashes/readEpicIdentity and storage.ts readEpicDefinitionCore) look only at DEF and ISSUE. A standalone LLD+PLAN item therefore has no hash in the candidate list, and resolveTaskRef reports unresolved-target. Adding an LLD head to one shared reader and to listEpicHashes closes this for both build phases.","evidence":"resolve.ts:150-163 listEpicHashes walks only DEF_RE and ISSUE_RE. resolve.ts:174-182 readEpicIdentity tries only `DEF-${h}.json` and `ISSUE-${h}.json`, and buildRef (:307-311) returns null without it. storage.ts:367-375 readEpicDefinitionCore loops over [defineArtifactId, issueArtifactId] only. implement.ts:61-62 and validate.ts:212-213 both call resolveTaskRef → resolveWorkflowRef (render.ts:54-55) and return 'unresolved-target' on a miss. The design changes all three readers, so both phases are covered. [files: src/workflow/tracker/resolve.ts, src/workflow/storage.ts, src/mcp/build-step/render.ts, src/mcp/build-step/phases/implement.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Triage never carries a specHash. decodeState rebuilds only runId/focus/repo, buildNextCall does not forward a spec, and the LLD already renders 'Seeded from' and stamps seededFromSpec whenever params.specHash is present.","evidence":"state.ts:32 `return { runId: s.runId, focus: s.focus, repo: s.repo };`. classify.ts:41-95 buildNextCall builds the design.story/define/issue params with no specHash. lld.ts:339-340 pushes '**Seeded from:** `SPEC-…`' when meta.seededFromSpec is set. orchestrator.ts:2320-2322 reads intent.params['specHash'] and :2354 stamps it. [files: src/mcp/triage-step/state.ts, src/mcp/triage-step/phases/classify.ts, src/workflow/artifacts/lld.ts, src/workflow/orchestrator.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"planMigration groups an item as 'standalone' only when a member carries the flag. Its label precedence is DEF → ISSUE → the first slug-carrying member in sorted-id order, with no LLD-specific step.","evidence":"migrate-docs-tree.ts:359 `members.some(m => m.standalone) ? 'standalone' : 'epic'`. :384-386 `slugOf(def) ?? slugOf(issue) ?? members.map(m => m.epicSlug).find(...)`, and the comment notes that BUILD- sorts before the others. The anchor at :368-372 also prefers any member's stamped epicCreatedAt over lld.createdAt, so the design's claim that the LLD now comes 'before any other member' must change the anchor as well as the label. [files: src/workflow/migrate-docs-tree.ts]","action":"When implementing step 4, also reorder the anchor at migrate-docs-tree.ts:368-372 so the LLD's epicCreatedAt/createdAt wins over another member's stamp for an anchorless item. The design text says this but lists only the label change in the migration steps.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The consumer list for readEpicDefinitionCore / readEpicCreatedAt / inheritedStoryStandalone under an LLD head is complete. Callers cited: orchestrator 1355/1817/2174/2331/2601/2611, tracker-auto 147/220, link 37, completion-record 58, standalone-record 267, validate 292-294.","evidence":"A grep for readEpicCreatedAt( found orchestrator.ts:1355, 1817, 2174, 2331, 2611, tracker-auto.ts:147, 220 and link.ts:37. There is no caller at :2601 (2583 is inheritedEpicSlug and 2611 is the readEpicCreatedAt call), so that citation is a harmless line slip. inheritedStoryStandalone( is called from validate.ts:294, standalone-record.ts:267, completion-record.ts:58 and also storage.ts:468 (storyRecordFolderArgs), which the design does not list. That site goes through the same head and buildRecordFolderArgs, so it behaves consistently with the design (reports true and files under docs/standalone). [files: src/workflow/orchestrator.ts, src/workflow/storage.ts, src/workflow/tracker-auto.ts, src/workflow/tracker/link.ts]","action":"Add storage.ts:468 storyRecordFolderArgs to §3.5's consumer list and drop the :2601 citation. No design change is needed.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The head-naming inputs exist: IssueBody has a title, and the standalone design.story params carry storyTitle from triage.","evidence":"artifacts/issue.ts:41-42 `readonly title: string;` (required). classify.ts:89 forwards storyTitle into the design.story params, and bugfix/next-after-issue.ts:82 does the same. finalizeStandaloneLld (orchestrator.ts:2298) currently uses inheritedEpicSlug(..., safeDeriveSlug(intent.focus)), the one site to switch to storyTitle-first. finalizeIssue/finalizeDefine/finalizeBrainstorm derive from focus at :716/:888/:1182. [files: src/workflow/artifacts/issue.ts, src/mcp/triage-step/phases/classify.ts, src/workflow/orchestrator.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.1","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Unscoped resolveByLabel returns today's winner or today's ambiguity refusal whenever a DEF/ISSUE item evidences the label. This holds only if LLD-headed hashes are kept out of the existing tiers and consulted last.","evidence":"resolve.ts:487-499 builds candidates from every hash in listEpicHashes, then picks from the explicit tier and then the implied tier. storyEvidence (:285-287) returns 'artifact' for any hash with an LLD/PLAN. If listEpicHashes simply appended LLD-only hashes, they would join the EXPLICIT tier and could turn today's unique winner into a refusal. The design avoids this by putting LLD-headed hashes in a separate last tier (§2.3, §3.6), so the invariant is reachable. The implementation must tag candidates by head kind and not rely on evidence rank alone. [files: src/workflow/tracker/resolve.ts]","action":"In the implementation, partition candidates by head kind (DEF/ISSUE vs LLD-only) before the explicit/implied loop. Do not just extend listEpicHashes and reuse the loop unchanged.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.2","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"BUILD/TESTS placement under docs/standalone is preserved through validate.ts resolveRouteFlag when an LLD becomes the head, because the LLD head reports standalone: true.","evidence":"validate.ts:292-294: noHead = Object.keys(readEpicDefinitionCore(...)).length === 0, then inheritedStoryStandalone(..., declared && noHead ? true : undefined). Today an LLD-only item has noHead = true and storage.ts:268-270 falls back to the LLD's own flag. After the change, noHead is false, but head.standalone is true (§2.1 postcondition), and inheritedStoryStandalone returns head.standalone first, so the result is still true. For a legacy unflagged LLD the result improves from undefined to true. The invariant holds provided readEpicDefinitionCore's 'readable' test (storage.ts:370) still accepts the LLD core. [files: src/mcp/build-step/phases/validate.ts, src/workflow/storage.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each acceptance criterion ac1-ac5 maps to at least one test that fails on today's code.","evidence":"ac1: resolveWorkflowRef on an LLD+PLAN-only fixture returns null today (listEpicHashes and readEpicIdentity are DEF/ISSUE only), so it fails before the fix. ac2: an unflagged LLD-only item reports standalone undefined today (storage.ts:268-270), so the docs/standalone placement test fails before the fix; the unchanged-epic suites act as regression guards. ac3: state.ts:32 drops any extra field and classify.ts never forwards specHash, so the round-trip and forwarding tests fail before the fix. ac4: finalizers derive from focus (orchestrator.ts:716/888/1182/2298), so title-based naming fails before the fix. ac5: migrate-docs-tree.ts:359/384-386 has no LLD precedence and no unflagged-standalone grouping, so the unit test fails before the fix. The 'Seeded from' test is correctly labelled a regression guard that passes before and after. [files: src/mcp/triage-step/state.ts, src/workflow/tracker/resolve.ts, src/workflow/migrate-docs-tree.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":8,"unverified":0},"template":"design-issue","reviewedAt":"2026-10-11T13:08:02.139Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
